WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.200
-Today is Friday, and that's
usually when I catch up

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.334
with some personal stuff.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.434
I check my in-box,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.434
and, of course,
send out thank-you notes.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:10.167
And I was running a bit
behind today,

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:11.534
so I thought if
you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.801
could I write out my weekly
thank-you notes right now?

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:17.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
During the show.

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:18.467
This will be perfect.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.467
Maybe if I can get some
thank-you-note-writing music

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:21.601
from happy James.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:22.634
Happy James?

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:25.133
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:29.567
He's so happy.
-Wow. That is happy James.

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:31.901
Aww!

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:33.100
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.200
-Thank you,
Ticketmaster crashing

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:37.734
because so many people wanted
Taylor Swift tickets.

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:40.167
Or as Ticketmaster put it,
"It's me.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.901
Hi.
I'm the problem. It's me."

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.067
[ Humming "Anti-Hero" ]
♪♪

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:55.767
That's a good jam.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:57.934
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:57.934 --> 00:01:00.434
Thank you,
airplane neck pillows,

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:03.767
for making it look like I fell
asleep in a velvet toilet.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.067
"Don't flush! Don't flush!"

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:12.367
-"Don't flush!
It's a velvet toilet."

00:01:12.367 --> 00:01:16.801
"He's so rich.
He had a velvet toilet."

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:18.968
[ Soft music playing, stops ]
Is your --

00:01:18.968 --> 00:01:20.267
[ Soft music playing, stops ]

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:21.634
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:25.601
-Thank you, Earth's population,
for hitting 8 billion.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:29.434
If we all chip in 6 bucks, we
can buy Twitter back from Elon.

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:32.434
Come on. Let's do it.
Let's do it! Come on!

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:34.534
[ Cheers and applause ]
I'm in.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.567
-Wow.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.701
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.400
-Thank you,
moving walkways at airports

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.901
for letting me get to my gate
a whole three seconds faster.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.167
I do go on them anyway, though.
-I do, too.

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:55.234
Even if they're broken.
-They're fun.

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:56.767
-Yeah.
-It's the future right there.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.734
-Yeah. I feel like the Jetsons.
-Yes!

00:01:58.734 --> 00:01:59.767
-Yeah.

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.067
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.868
-Thank you, "Yellowstone,"
for proving that

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:10.300
parents can figure out
streaming apps.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:11.901
♪♪
-Come on!

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:14.801
-Good joke.
-Yeah. Topical. Yeah.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.634
-Peacock.
-Yeah. Peacock, man.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.801
-Peacock all the way, man.

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.334
-The P.

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.767
-Peacock -- your nickname,
you call it "The P"?

00:02:24.767 --> 00:02:26.667
-Yeah, well, it's better than
the other one.

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.634
♪♪

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:39.067
It's a family show.

00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:40.267
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.701
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:44.701
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.501
-You got me on that one.
You gotta make a T-shirt.

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:53.167
We gotta make
a T-shirt, right?

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:54.934
-If they knew what --
That's what's up.

00:02:54.934 --> 00:02:57.133
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.
I know, I know.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:02:59.300
You just -- Yeah, the people
at Peacock are like,

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:02.334
"He's onto something."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:03.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.033
-Oh, man.

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.234
[ Soft music playing ]

00:03:06.234 --> 00:03:09.067
Thank you, Friendsgiving,
for being when friends

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.167
gather together with
a turkey, three sides,

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:13.234
and 20 bottles of cheap wine.

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:14.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:16.100
Yeah.

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:21.501
-"I brought the wine!"

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.601
[ Soft music playing ]

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.834
-Thank you,
French's Fried Onions,

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.667
for figuring out
the secret to getting people

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:30.200
to eat green beans is putting
a different, better food on top.

00:03:33.801 --> 00:03:36.501
"That was Yummy, I need more.
What's the secret?"

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.701
"Uh, I put Doritos all over it."

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:41.067
-"Oh, my God! Delicious."

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:42.634
-Mwah!

00:03:42.634 --> 00:03:44.033
Oh, yeah, this is good.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.734
[ Soft music playing ]

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:48.167
Thank you, Thanksgiving,
or as the fold-out tables

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:52.734
in your garage put it,
"Our time to shine, bish."

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.467
There you have it.
Those are our "Thank You Notes."

